NLTK -> natural language toolkit
tools in nltk
---TOKENIZATION--
->splits text into words or sentences
*sentence:"I love AI."
*tokenization:["I", "love", "AI", "."]
->types 
word tokenization->split text into words
*Example:
"Machine Learning is fun."→["Machine", "Learning", "is", "fun", "."]
sentence tokenization->split text into sentence
*Example:
"Hello. How are you?"→["Hello.", "How are you?"]
---STOP WORDS---
->stop words are the words that do not add much meaning to a  sentence , they are removed during NLP
-> is,am,are,the,a,an,in,on,of,and are the stop word
*Example
Sentence:"The cat is sitting on the mat."
After removing stop words:
["cat", "sitting", "mat"]
---stemming---
-> proccess of removing prefiexs or suffixes to get the root word
-> the root word may not be a valid english word
*example running -> run
studies->studi
--lemmatization--
->conert a word into its dictionary form using vocabulary and grammer
*example playing-> play
Running->run
better-> good
studies->study
->output is always meaningfull
---TEXT VECTORIZATION---
->convert text into number so computer can understand
-> vector is simply a list of numbers that represent text
-> the computer converts text into numbers using a vocabulary(dictionary)
-> the computer list all the unique words and  number them 
->replace words with numbers
-> we use SKLEARN beause it provide ready-made tools to convert text into vector
->ONE-HOT ENCODING->converts words into binary vectors(0s and 1s),where 1 indicates the presence of word and 0 indicates its absence.
---POS Tagging---
->pos tagging is the proces of identifying the grammatical role  of each word in a sentence
->TAG
NN- noun*book
NNP- proper Noun *ram
VB- verb *play
VBG- verb(-ing form)*playing
VBZ → Verb (is/plays/eats)
JJ → Adjective*tall
RB → Adverb
PRP → Pronoun
DT → Article (the, a, an)
IN → Preposition
CC → Conjunction
CD → Number
